cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or software, please cite it as below."
title: "TENOR: an open benchmark for meeting note-takers (Transcripts, Evidence, Notes, Outcomes, Recall)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lakhani
    given-names: Kian
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  TENOR is an open benchmark for meeting note-takers. It replays public meetings
  (the AMI Meeting Corpus, CC BY 4.0) into real products and measures, from the
  outside, whether the meeting was captured, whether the notes are faithful and
  complete, whether answers about it are right, and what is lost when transcripts
  are deleted. Granola and Wispr Flow are the reference products. Also includes
  the archived Northwind synthetic benchmark and Concentrate reference memory.
  Independent research prototype, not affiliated with Granola or Wispr.
keywords:
  - meeting note-takers
  - benchmark
  - evaluation
  - meeting transcripts
  - AMI Meeting Corpus
  - LLM-as-judge calibration
